{"parentUuid":"aefa65ae-ca9b-42b8-b774-3b1169c68546","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a6b3d1e0-26c3-4654-89ef-5b4030b63c3f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MtyJeUPUpBzQUwoY6HBK1R","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Title: MetaHuman Animator Markerless Motion Capture Plugin on macOS Matthieu Huguet\nURL: http://localhost:4100\nSource element: <article>\n---\nMetaHuman Animator Markerless Motion Capture Plugin on macOS\nEveryone says the body capture is Windows only. It is not. The blocker is one stale number, and here is the whole chain from a video clip to an animation.\n\nShort answer: it works. Epic's markerless body capture runs on an Apple Silicon Mac, and the reason almost everyone believes otherwise is a stale build identifier, not a platform restriction. I tested the whole chain end to end on 22 August 2026 and got an animation out.\n\nThe plugin belongs to Epic Games. It ships with Unreal Engine and none of its code is mine. My contribution is narrow and I want it stated plainly: I compiled it on macOS and ran it end to end on a real clip until an animation came out. It works.\n\nSetup: macOS on Apple Silicon, Unreal Engine 5.8.1 as an Installed Build from the Launcher, Xcode 26.6. Input was four seconds of gameplay footage at 3840x2160 and 60 frames per second. Output was 239 tracked frames after five processing stages, in about thirty minutes.\n\nWhy everyone thinks it is Windows only\n\nEnable the plugin and the editor greets you with this:\n\nThe following modules are missing or built with a different engine version:\n  MetaHumanBodyTracker\n  BodyTracker\n  Segmentation\n  MetaHumanBodyOptimizer\n\nEngine modules cannot be compiled at runtime. Please build through your IDE.\n\nIt reads like a platform wall. It is not one. Three facts, each checkable in a minute:\n\nThe .uplugin declares no PlatformAllowList at all.\nNo Build.cs restricts the platform.\nThe Binaries/Mac folder already contains universal arm64 and x86_64 dylibs.\n\nThe real cause is one number. The plugin's module manifest announced build 54595663 while the engine expected 55116800. It was compiled against an earlier 5.8, and the editor rejects any module whose build identifier does not match. Nothing about macOS is involved.\n\nThe fix, and the one sentence that carries it\n\nAn engine plugin cannot be recompiled inside an Installed Build. A project plugin can. That asymmetry is the entire solution. Move the plugin out of the engine and into the project, drop its stale binaries, and build the project target.\n\nmv \"$UE/Engine/Plugins/Marketplace/MetaHumanBodyTracker_5.8\" \\\n   \"$PROJECT/Plugins/MetaHumanBodyTracker\"\nrm -rf \"$PROJECT/Plugins/MetaHumanBodyTracker/Binaries\" \\\n       \"$PROJECT/Plugins/MetaHumanBodyTracker/Intermediate\"\n\n\"$UE/Engine/Build/BatchFiles/Mac/Build.sh\" MyProjectEditor Mac Development \\\n  -project=\"$PROJECT/MyProject.uproject\" -waitmutex\n\nRes\n\n[truncated to 2500 chars]"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nTab Context:\n- Executed on tabId: seed\n- Available tabs:\n  • tabId seed: \"MetaHuman Animator Markerless Motion Capture Plugin on macOS Matthieu Huguet\" (http://localhost:4100)"}]}]},"uuid":"2abad224-abc6-4e2a-948f-b52c6363b5c8","timestamp":"2026-08-22T13:52:55.473Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"Title: MetaHuman Animator Markerless Motion Capture Plugin on macOS Matthieu Huguet\nURL: http://localhost:4100\nSource element: <article>\n---\nMetaHuman Animator Markerless Motion Capture Plugin on macOS\nEveryone says the body capture is Windows only. It is not. The blocker is one stale number, and here is the whole chain from a video clip to an animation.\n\nShort answer: it works. Epic's markerless body capture runs on an Apple Silicon Mac, and the reason almost everyone believes otherwise is a stale build identifier, not a platform restriction. I tested the whole chain end to end on 22 August 2026 and got an animation out.\n\nThe plugin b